{"name":"Silly Puddy","hex":"#f4b0bb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Laughable or amusing through foolishness or a foolish appearance.","Absurdly large."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Sillily: in a silly manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silly"},{"term":"puddy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Pronunciation spelling of pussy (“cat”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puddy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silly Putty","blocks":[{"text":"Silly Putty is a toy containing silicone polymers that has unusual physical properties. It can flow like a liquid, bounce and can be stretched or broken depending on the amount of physical stress to which it is subjected. It contains viscoelastic liquid silicones, a type of non-Newtonian fluid, which makes it act as a viscous liquid over a long period of time but as an elastic solid over a short time period. It was originally created during research into a potential rubber substitute for use by the United States in World War II."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Big_dsc05433.jpg/330px-Big_dsc05433.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silly_Putty"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Silly_putty_dripping.jpg/500px-Silly_putty_dripping.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Silly_putty_dripping.jpg/1280px-Silly_putty_dripping.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Silly_putty_dripping.jpg/500px-Silly_putty_dripping.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silly Putty flowing through a hole","link":"https://en.wikipedia.